KG42.register("rules-88a63601c47922e86da9ae00",{"id":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market::v141-c-R008","paper":"43-operating_envelope_ev_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R008","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-lem","name":"Prosumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Prosumers may participate in decentralized peer trading within DOEs without explicit DSO engagement in price settlement. Scope: Decentralized prosumer participation in peer trading in the proposed LEM. Condition: Within the DOEs. Prosumers can decide whether to participate in P2P trading or trade with the upstream grid. Scope: Prosumer choice of P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid. Condition: The participation decision is made by generating buying/selling bids within DOEs.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.prosumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.prosumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Decentralized prosumer participation in peer trading in the proposed LEM. | Prosumer choice of P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g02-E27"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Prosumers may participate in decentralized peer trading within DOEs without explicit DSO engagement in price settlement. Scope: Decentralized prosumer participation in peer trading in the proposed LEM. Condition: Within the DOEs.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E04"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Prosumers can decide whether to participate in P2P trading or trade with the upstream grid. Scope: Prosumer choice of P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid. Condition: The participation decision is made by generating buying/selling bids within DOEs.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E04","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M03-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"Related Works","anchor_text":"of the PV pr m imports/exports and securing network operations. Prosumers in can participate in the ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Prosumers can participate in the LEM to trade energy with their peers in a decentralized fashion within the DOEs without the explicit engagement of the DSO in price settlement. Peer-to-peer (P2P) trading is such kind of technique that allows prosumers to trade in the LEM at their preferred prices and reduce their energy costs by having access to less expensive energy. It also enables DER owners to increase their bilateral trading and meet up the energy demand locally [28]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","location":{"location_id":"src-1fe7e180ad-p07-c2r1__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"Prosumers Bidding Strategy","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON SMART GRID, VOL. 15, NO. 2, MARCH 2024 lem tou lem ad min Ppbj,t · j,t + Pgbj,t","equation_id":"(28)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Prosumers can decide on their participation in the P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid by generating their bids for buying/selling energy within DOEs. Each prosumer decides on the trading bids and submits them to the LEM in each τ by the proposed bidding strategy. In this case, the objective of prosumer is to minimize the total trading cost as, min ∑_{j∈J} (P^{pb}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gb}_{j,t}·Λ^{tou}_{j,t} + P^{ps}_{j,t}·Λ^{lem}_{j,t} + P^{gs}_{j,t}·Λ^{fit}_{t}) τ; P^{ps}_{j,t}, P^{gs}_{j,t} ≤ 0, ∀j∈J,∀t∈T, subject to: (29)−(35), (28) where the first and second terms in (28) refer to the total cost of buying energy from the peers and the upstream grid, respectively and the third and fourth terms define the total profit of selling energy to the peers and the upstream grid in the LEM, respectively. Here, P^{pb}_{j,t}/P^{ps}_{j,t} and P^{gb}_{j,t}/P^{gs}_{j,t} are buying/selling quantities of prosumer j with the peers and the upstream grid in each τ, respectively; and Λ^{tou}_{j,t} are the time-of-use (ToU) buying prices with the upstream grid."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational variable is declared for this participation rule. The source evidence states a permission and a discrete trading choice, but it does not define a standalone participation-decision variable in R008; the bid quantities in the quoted Eq. (28) evidence belong to the separate bidding-rule scope.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed input or constant is defined for this participation rule. DOE limits, bid prices, and quantities appear in the quoted bidding material for context, but they are not declared parameters of R008's frozen graph and cannot be assigned to this rule without revision."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-bidding","v141-a-M03-participation","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E04","quote":"Prosumers can participate in the LEM to trade energy with their peers in a decentralized fashion within the DOEs without the explicit engagement of the DSO in price settlement."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E27","quote":"Prosumers can decide on their participation in the P2P trading or trading with the upstream grid by generating their bids for buying/selling energy within DOEs."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"e1f1df5b881fef9bd221f0790cafbb00391ff5dab8903ec10580a137a1648522","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"R008 is a participation/admission rule: it states that prosumers may participate in decentralized peer trading within DOEs without the DSO explicitly engaging in price settlement, and that they may choose between P2P trading and trading with the upstream grid by generating buying/selling bids within DOEs. The frozen graph contains only the unary node participation.prosumer, with no declared participation decision variable, bid quantity, price, DOE, or optimization object for this rule. The only nearby mathematical content supplied with C002 is Eq. (28), the prosumer bidding objective, which belongs to the bidding-rule scope and cannot be imported into R008 without changing the frozen graph. The existing constraints are therefore retained as procedural and not_formalized; no x/theta objects are declared for this rule.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is a unary permission attaching to the participation.prosumer node: prosumers may engage in decentralized peer trading within DOEs without explicit DSO price settlement. No graph edge is supplied or needed for this permission statement."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 states the participation choice and its operational route for the same prosumer participation node: choose P2P or upstream-grid trading by generating buying/selling bids within DOEs. The frozen R008 graph has no edge representing this choice, so no edge_id is asserted."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
